$split_video — scene split via frame average-hash diffs

SUMMARY
  Reads each videos[] file, compares consecutive frame average hashes
  (imagehash.average_hash), splits where diff > threshold, merges fragments
  shorter than min_frames using adjacent-small or boundary-hash rules, and
  writes one MP4 per fragment to videos[] with labels[] metadata.

SYNTAX
  $split_video
  $split_video(threshold=12, hash_size=8, min_frames=100)

INPUT
  videos[] — source video files

OUTPUT
  videos[] — one MP4 per fragment (input videos cleared)
  labels[] — one "fragment" entry per output video:
    [ "fragment", [("videos", "<link>")], {"src": "<source_link>", "frame": <start>} ]

ARGUMENTS
  threshold=  — split when abs(hash - prev_hash) > threshold (default 10)
  hash_size=  — average_hash size (default 8)
  min_frames= — merge fragments shorter than this (default 100)

MERGE RULES (fragments with size < min_frames)
  1. Join with the next fragment when both are shorter than min_frames.
  2. Otherwise compare boundary hashes with previous/next neighbor and join
     to the side with the smaller diff.

DEPENDENCIES
  opencv-python, Pillow, imagehash, ffmpeg.
  uv sync --extra split_video   or   uv sync --extra media + imagehash

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_SPLIT_VIDEO=1 — placeholder MP4 + labels, no ffmpeg/imagehash work.

EXAMPLE
  @parts: $file('long_clip.mp4') -> $split_video(threshold=10) -> $save('frag_%04d.mp4')

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No — replaces videos[] with fragments; manages labels[] directly.
